                <pb facs="0858" n="1692" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1308</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-02T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 3, 9.37 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1631. For War Trade Board [from Smith]:</p>
                <p>Please refer to my cipher telegram of July 30 [<hi rendition="#italic">31</hi>],
                    No. 168 [<hi rendition="#italic">1608</hi>]. Have now completed Bilbao
                    investigation. Have privately [conferred] with representative shipowners.
                    Believe that in own interests proposition number 2, but more likely number 3,
                    mentioned in my cipher telegram [acceptable] to them. Believe that Government
                    would privately consent to private charter to United States through approved
                    commercial agency. Basis of charter full capacity of ship on agreed rates [per
                    ton] cargo weight or measurement according to destination American ports to
                    French Atlantic, French Mediterranean, or Italian ports. Owners are now studying
                    whether suitable tonnage is available and not needed for Spanish requirements,
                    also considering charter rates. I would appreciate your views in order to guide
                    me in further conferences; also advise minimum block tonnage you would consider.
                    Smith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
